{
 "source": "function Unresolved_dd62ed3e(address arg0, uint256 arg1) public view returns (uint256) {\n        require(0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x40);\n        return storage_map_b[arg0][address(uint160(arg1))];\n    }",
 "notes": "allowance read returned 0x (no return value) while reference returns 0x14 = 50, the amount set by approve (entrypoint_16 writes storage_map_b[owner][spender]). Changed the function to view returning uint256 and indexed the nested mapping with address(uint160(arg1)) so the second parameter is treated as the spender address; this fixes the previous compile error (uint256 used as mapping key where address expected) and returns the allowance written by approve, matching the reference return 0x14 after approve(50) and transferFrom(30)."
}
